    "q-94153": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94153",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})^{2}+(-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-94153-a",
