    "q-94173": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94173",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the first equation for ${x}_{2}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}+(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}){y}_{1}+2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8{y}_{1}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =12{y}_{1}^{2}-9{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-94173-a",
