    "q-140941": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140941",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
